WEBVTT

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:29.440
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:29.440
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:29.440
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:53.720 --> 00:02:03.290
Chapter X

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:10.470
On November 10th
of Space Year 788...

00:02:10.470 --> 00:02:15.570
...in the POW camp on Planet Econia,
Lt. Commander Yang Wenli had just arrived...

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:17.450
...and was facing an unexpected
threat to his life.

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:37.770
What's going on ?!

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:41.690
It looks like Costea is
finally getting started.

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:46.750
He seems intent on {disposing of} abandoning
those who are undesirable to him.

00:02:47.770 --> 00:02:51.460
If he throws me in carelessly,
I could be in a fix.{get stuck.}

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:53.550
He probably should think twice.

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:58.180
Costea, you bastard !

00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:00.850
Trying to kill us,
along with his people ?

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:04.650
Now I'll survive at all costs
and make him pay for this !

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:08.020
Costea feels cornered...

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:09.120
...by you.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:10.040
Me ?

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:10.760
Yes.

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:11.610
Don't you see...

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:13.870
...Hero of El Facil ?

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:20.210
He must have thought that I was a secret inspector or something.

00:03:21.770 --> 00:03:23.060
He has totally
overestimated me.

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:27.980
I think so, too.

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:32.350
Costea saw the presence of the
entire military establishment in you.

00:03:33.590 --> 00:03:40.120
When one has something to hide one always fears shadows and tends to overreact in self-defense.

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:52.590
That's a great
lecture, Captain.

00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:56.030
But could you also instruct us
on what we should do now ?

00:03:56.950 --> 00:04:01.970
Well first, we must get
out of this situation alive.

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:07.560
To use a flattering expression, Yang Wenli was a deliberate and thoughtful person...

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:10.990
...but he was not always
improvisational or adaptive.

00:04:10.990 --> 00:04:15.310
In this instance, what he chose to do was as effective as it was simple.

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:22.550
Well then, Captain Kefenhiller,
can you lead us out of here right away ?

00:04:23.210 --> 00:04:24.790
You're talking strangely.

00:04:24.790 --> 00:04:28.970
As I said before, I don't have the power to do something like that.

00:04:28.970 --> 00:04:30.370
From my perspective...

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:35.650
...I don't think you'd come here in the first
place without preparing an evacuation route.

00:04:36.260 --> 00:04:39.650
That's called "overestimation," young man.

00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:43.300
Captain, you're too humble.

00:04:54.740 --> 00:04:59.150
Captain, you might not have a lingering attachment to what little time you have left in your life...

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:02.650
...but for Lt. Commander Yang,
his future is much longer than his past.

00:05:03.270 --> 00:05:05.540
Plus, he has a
very promising future.

00:05:05.540 --> 00:05:10.050
If you help him, I'm sure
it'll be to your benefit, too.

00:05:11.570 --> 00:05:16.220
And if you help me too, your
good deed will reach perfection.

00:05:17.070 --> 00:05:17.900
How about it ?

00:05:36.370 --> 00:05:37.720
It's an impulse-generating device.

00:05:38.590 --> 00:05:39.470
It looks handmade.

00:05:46.250 --> 00:05:49.810
It's a communication tunnel. It hasn't been used for the last 15 years.

00:05:50.790 --> 00:05:53.070
It runs everywhere underground.

00:05:53.070 --> 00:05:56.020
Let us go down there
and avoid the danger.

00:05:57.570 --> 00:05:58.320
All of you !

00:05:58.320 --> 00:05:59.460
I won't let you do
what you please !

00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:17.640
If they're going to get in our way,
I'm going to make trouble for them.

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:18.560
Please go ahead and go.

00:06:24.760 --> 00:06:29.160
I didn't realize Lieutenant
Patorichev had such brute strength.

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:32.120
He ripped apart
the handcuffs !

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:34.380
No, actually,
I can do that, too.

00:06:35.960 --> 00:06:37.800
I see, it's a trick.

00:06:39.110 --> 00:06:44.720
Hey, you brave escapees,
you can come with us if you like.

00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:46.100
But I won't force
you, of course.

00:06:55.090 --> 00:06:55.870
We have no choice.

00:07:40.410 --> 00:07:43.430
If you had used this, you could
have escaped, couldn't you ?

00:07:43.820 --> 00:07:48.110
I like to plan things,
but I hate to fail.

00:07:48.110 --> 00:07:51.320
Rather than actually taking action,
I end up hesitating to do it.

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:53.970
But under the circumstances,
I don't have a choice.

00:07:53.970 --> 00:07:57.750
It doesn't feel good to
let Costea triumph, either.

00:07:57.750 --> 00:08:00.710
I'd prefer him
to cry in pain.

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:07.530
Where does this tunnel lead ?

00:08:09.220 --> 00:08:11.100
You shouldn't try to know
everything that's ahead.

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:13.320
Or else it'll
spoil the fun.

00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:22.300
I can't hear the
explosions anymore.

00:08:22.870 --> 00:08:25.270
Next up are ground soldiers
rushing in, I suppose.

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:29.490
Since this is a rural place,
plans tend to be coarse...

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:32.370
...and that's a pity.

00:08:33.020 --> 00:08:36.100
I'd like the Superintendent
to plan things more carefully.

00:08:37.150 --> 00:08:40.620
If he gets too sophisticated, our window of opportunity will get smaller.

00:08:41.570 --> 00:08:42.670
It's better this way.

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:48.540
Lt. Junior Grade, you shouldn't have carried on with your bad acting.

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:50.860
It's one way of living to follow the given role and die in it...

00:08:50.860 --> 00:08:53.330
...but I suppose you'd be too ashamed to be able to face your ancestors...

00:08:53.430 --> 00:08:57.550
...if someone wrote an undesirable epitaph for you and you weren't alive to complain about it, right ?

00:09:02.430 --> 00:09:05.550
I wasn't acting.

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:11.910
The Superintendent promised that if we
cooperated, he would grant us amnesty...

00:09:11.910 --> 00:09:15.100
...and return us home to
the Empire in six months.

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:23.740
To be able to return home - it must be the ultimate temptation for a prisoner.

00:09:23.740 --> 00:09:28.310
Even if there were doubts about it, hope would outweigh the doubt.

00:09:28.310 --> 00:09:30.380
I suppose I can't blame him{the prisoner}.

00:09:31.380 --> 00:09:35.200
So what did Captain Costea
say he was planning to do ?

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:36.520
That's...

00:09:38.740 --> 00:09:44.000
I was told that he was going to disclose the many secret wrongdoings of Captain Kefenhiller.

00:09:45.460 --> 00:09:47.970
I see, my wrongdoings...

00:09:51.210 --> 00:09:55.100
So you willingly took
Captain Costea's offer.

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:04.470
I'll say this on my honor
as an Imperial soldier.

00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:07.880
I had no intention of cooperating
with Costea's petty scheme.

00:10:07.880 --> 00:10:10.610
I have definitely not done anything
to disgrace my family name.

00:10:11.130 --> 00:10:15.450
In other words, you were
tricked by Costea all along.

00:10:17.900 --> 00:10:19.590
You shouldn't feel ashamed.

00:10:19.590 --> 00:10:22.570
The Superintendent was more
unscrupulous than you were.

00:10:22.570 --> 00:10:28.030
Oh well, I never knew I'd end up bad-mouthing my superior to cheer up the enemy.

00:10:29.240 --> 00:10:33.620
Captain, you seem to know a lot about the circumstances surrounding us.

00:10:33.620 --> 00:10:39.260
So I suppose you know what to do
about the current state of things, right ?

00:10:39.260 --> 00:10:43.830
I just instigate things - I leave
the cleaning up to young people.

00:10:44.310 --> 00:10:46.920
I provided the escape route...

00:10:46.920 --> 00:10:52.160
...so I don't suppose I'll be punished for expecting you to make good use of what's given.

00:10:55.090 --> 00:10:56.130
Oh, well.

00:10:56.130 --> 00:10:59.020
I somehow graduated
from the military academy...

00:10:59.020 --> 00:11:02.300
...but I feel like I'm being verbally quizzed by an old examiner.

00:11:13.640 --> 00:11:15.840
Well, we'll climb up here.

00:11:16.600 --> 00:11:18.540
Then we'll reach the exit.

00:11:27.920 --> 00:11:31.370
Well, things are getting
strange, aren't they ?

00:11:31.370 --> 00:11:32.250
I agree.

00:11:32.800 --> 00:11:35.600
What a shrewd old man.

00:11:35.600 --> 00:11:37.770
If he wasn't a prisoner...

00:11:37.770 --> 00:11:40.030
...I'd guess he would have been a part of the nucleus of the Empire brains now...

00:11:40.030 --> 00:11:43.990
...and would be scheming
many plots against our forces.

00:11:46.850 --> 00:11:48.190
I feel the same way.

00:11:48.190 --> 00:11:52.370
If that old man were an Imperial Fleet Admiral or High Admiral...

00:11:52.370 --> 00:11:54.750
...our forces could
have been easy prey.

00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:59.300
This could be one actual example that history has many different possibilities.

00:12:04.930 --> 00:12:09.550
Captain, it seems that Captain Costea thinks of me as his enemy...

00:12:09.550 --> 00:12:13.130
...but should I assume that this entire camp is against me ?

00:12:13.130 --> 00:12:15.350
It's all up to each soldier's judgement.

00:12:16.110 --> 00:12:19.620
Whether they'll blindly follow their 
superior or they'll decide to follow reason.

00:12:19.620 --> 00:12:23.400
Our fate depends on
that, I would think.

00:12:25.740 --> 00:12:28.620
It will be interesting, to see what soldiers will choose to do...

00:12:28.620 --> 00:12:32.750
...in a military organization
under a democratic society.

00:12:33.640 --> 00:12:36.770
In an autocratic nation, soldiers have
no choice but to follow their superiors.

00:12:36.770 --> 00:12:40.020
But in a democratic society that
values free will and individualism...

00:12:40.020 --> 00:12:43.470
...each soldier ought to be able to judge good and evil on his own.

00:12:43.470 --> 00:12:45.020
I guess that's what
he means to say.

00:12:45.020 --> 00:12:48.130
It pains me that I can't definitively say that {i.e. each soldier being able to judge good and evil on his own} is how it will be.

00:13:02.700 --> 00:13:04.260
Where's Lt. Commander Yang ?

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:05.770
Find Kefenhiller !

00:13:06.430 --> 00:13:08.510
Find them both,
at all costs !

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:10.370
Captain Costea...

00:13:14.830 --> 00:13:15.870
Oh, well.

00:13:15.870 --> 00:13:19.980
The true ruler of this planet
might actually be this old man.

00:13:32.320 --> 00:13:33.620
Where's Lt. Commander Yang ?!

00:13:33.620 --> 00:13:35.000
How about Kefenhiller ?!

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:36.950
You can't find them
because of the rubble ?!

00:13:37.230 --> 00:13:38.270
I don't care
if they're dead !

00:13:38.270 --> 00:13:39.990
Just find them fast !

00:13:39.990 --> 00:13:41.800
Are you saying the room
is too badly damaged ?!

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:45.060
Even if they're crushed, Patorichev is large,
so you could at least identify him, right ?

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:52.240
Hello, Honored Superintendent.

00:13:52.880 --> 00:13:56.200
I'm honored to hear you're
worried about my well-being.

00:13:58.170 --> 00:13:59.550
C...can't be...

00:13:59.550 --> 00:14:03.310
I thought I would
receive a compliment.

00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:11.200
After all, this humble Fyodor Patorichev has
arrested and hauled in the despicable escapees.

00:14:13.020 --> 00:14:13.810
Presberg !

00:14:14.930 --> 00:14:17.450
I can't believe these
guys are actually alive.

00:14:24.990 --> 00:14:25.920
Lt. Commander Yang...

00:14:27.220 --> 00:14:31.490
Please, Captain, don't
make me pull the trigger.

00:14:31.490 --> 00:14:36.810
Bringing myself honor by shooting my superior isn't what I want.

00:14:40.160 --> 00:14:42.130
This is practically a bluff.

00:14:42.130 --> 00:14:46.620
If the Captain moves swiftly, my shots probably won't hit him, given my shooting skills.

00:14:46.620 --> 00:14:48.660
But he doesn't know
how unskilled I am.

00:15:02.970 --> 00:15:06.600
Lt. Commander Yang, do you
realize what you're doing ?

00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:12.400
I think I do, but I also see that there
may be room for another interpretation.

00:15:13.280 --> 00:15:14.810
Interpretation ?!

00:15:14.810 --> 00:15:17.000
There's no room
for interpretation !

00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:19.730
I'll tell you the
unmistakable facts !

00:15:19.730 --> 00:15:23.870
You - you are pointing
a gun at your superior !

00:15:23.870 --> 00:15:25.720
This is what's called mutiny !

00:15:25.720 --> 00:15:26.620
Do you understand that ?

00:15:27.170 --> 00:15:31.460
Well, as far as I'm concerned,
I understand it to be an act of self-defense.

00:15:31.460 --> 00:15:32.860
How is it self-defense ?!

00:15:33.290 --> 00:15:35.570
A trench mortar vs. a rifle.

00:15:35.570 --> 00:15:39.560
My action is much lesser in scale than yours,
so much so, that it's kind of cute, don't you think ?

00:15:39.960 --> 00:15:40.960
What's cute about it ?!

00:15:45.600 --> 00:15:46.720
Costea !

00:15:46.720 --> 00:15:48.990
You dirty little bastard !

00:15:50.620 --> 00:15:52.170
Presberg, listen to me.

00:15:52.680 --> 00:15:54.170
I have no reason to listen !

00:16:03.370 --> 00:16:06.290
You !
You bastard !

00:16:06.290 --> 00:16:08.370
Help...help me...

00:16:08.370 --> 00:16:10.970
Are you going to hang
 your superior out to dry ?

00:16:12.130 --> 00:16:17.310
Captain, if you're killed by
LTJG Presberg, we'll avenge your death.

00:16:17.310 --> 00:16:23.320
That way, everything will be fine, and no one'll get hurt.

00:16:23.320 --> 00:16:26.620
So you don't have to
worry about anything else.

00:16:26.620 --> 00:16:30.270
I...acknowledge...
I acknowledge my wrongdoing...

00:16:30.270 --> 00:16:33.490
So do something about
Presberg...please !

00:16:35.120 --> 00:16:39.060
So you're saying you want to be
alive for a court martial, correct ?

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:40.340
Yes, I want to
be court martialed...

00:16:40.340 --> 00:16:42.970
I want to be alive
for a court martial...

00:16:47.680 --> 00:16:49.220
That's quite honorable of you.

00:16:49.220 --> 00:16:53.700
Well, I guess I'll have to ensure the safety
of an important witness for the court martial.

00:17:25.690 --> 00:17:28.690
As Yang got the situation under control...

00:17:28.690 --> 00:17:33.320
...he also reported to the Thanatos Police Headquarters in charge of this star system.

00:17:36.740 --> 00:17:40.360
I am Military Police Commander
Commodore Matthewson.

00:17:40.360 --> 00:17:42.120
You must be Lt. Commander Yang Wenli, correct ?

00:17:42.120 --> 00:17:43.620
I have heard of you.

00:17:44.370 --> 00:17:46.640
If I remember correctly, you are
the Hero of El Facil, are you not ?

00:17:46.940 --> 00:17:48.290
I'm flattered.

00:17:48.740 --> 00:17:50.200
Is he being sarcastic ?

00:17:50.200 --> 00:17:52.550
I didn't go to greet the Military
Police Department, after all.

00:17:54.220 --> 00:17:56.650
And you are Lt. Patorichev, correct ?

00:17:57.040 --> 00:17:58.830
It's been a long time, Commodore.

00:17:59.520 --> 00:18:02.850
So I hear there has been
some kind of commotion.

00:18:02.850 --> 00:18:05.020
I want to know the details.

00:18:05.020 --> 00:18:09.490
In the first place, why is the newly appointed Secretary reporting, rather than the Superintendent ?

00:18:10.400 --> 00:18:14.130
Um...it's difficult
to explain, but...

00:18:14.130 --> 00:18:17.450
It may be difficult for
Lt. Commander Yang to explain.

00:18:17.450 --> 00:18:20.060
May I offer the
explanation in his place ?

00:18:21.270 --> 00:18:21.800
Yes.

00:18:23.490 --> 00:18:24.620
To tell you the truth...

00:18:24.620 --> 00:18:28.120
...Lt. Commander Yang was directly
ordered by the Chief General Staff Office...

00:18:28.120 --> 00:18:30.840
...to come to Econia POW
camp for an inspection.

00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:32.260
What ?

00:18:32.260 --> 00:18:36.880
It was because Superintendent Costea was
under suspicion of public fund embezzlement.

00:18:36.880 --> 00:18:39.500
Unfortunately, that
suspicion was confirmed.

00:18:39.500 --> 00:18:42.430
What was worse, Superintendent Costea
learned of Lt. Commander Yang's true mission...

00:18:42.430 --> 00:18:44.800
...and fearing that he might be
exposed for his wrongdoing...

00:18:44.800 --> 00:18:48.790
...tried to kill Lt. Commander Yang in the confusion of a staged prisoner riot.

00:18:50.820 --> 00:18:52.480
That sounds odd.

00:18:52.480 --> 00:18:54.370
It's not just
for this camp...

00:18:54.370 --> 00:18:57.620
...but the rights of inspection lie with the National Defense Ministry...

00:18:57.620 --> 00:18:59.340
...not with the Chief
General Staff Office.

00:18:59.910 --> 00:19:01.770
What is he going to do if
the Commodore points that out ?

00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:06.520
It seems the Commodore is
not presently aware of it.

00:19:07.320 --> 00:19:10.470
Initially, Vice-Superintendent Commander Jennings...

00:19:10.470 --> 00:19:13.250
...and his officers were taken hostage
while on their night patrol...

00:19:13.250 --> 00:19:16.880
...and Lt. Commander Yang and I were
directed to be their substitutes.

00:19:16.880 --> 00:19:20.850
And then, Captain Costea took a
hard-line action and tried to kill us all...

00:19:20.850 --> 00:19:24.250
...along with the prisoners who
were informed of the plan.

00:19:24.250 --> 00:19:28.250
Fortunately, we won the cooperation of the prisoners, so we were able to escape...

00:19:28.250 --> 00:19:31.020
...and turning the tables,
took Captain Costea into custody.

00:19:31.020 --> 00:19:32.370
That is the explanation
of the circumstances.

00:19:33.570 --> 00:19:35.920
At this point, I'll have to follow the Lieutenant's scenario.

00:19:37.930 --> 00:19:41.810
We first have to fulfill our objective,
and the explanations can wait till later.

00:19:43.060 --> 00:19:45.330
For the time being, I will accept your account of the situation.

00:19:45.330 --> 00:19:51.470
I will send my agent down there,
so follow his orders from now on.

00:19:51.470 --> 00:19:54.030
He's Military Police Office
Secretary, Commander Murai.

00:19:56.860 --> 00:19:58.160
I'm Murai.

00:19:58.160 --> 00:20:00.470
Lt. Commander Yang, I understand
about the Superintendent...

00:20:00.470 --> 00:20:02.120
...but how about
Vice-Superintendent ?

00:20:02.120 --> 00:20:05.810
Commander Jennings is injured
and is now in the infirmary.

00:20:05.810 --> 00:20:07.350
Injured ?

00:20:07.350 --> 00:20:10.380
The Commander was initially taken
hostage by the prisoners, so...

00:20:12.000 --> 00:20:13.400
I heard that already.

00:20:13.400 --> 00:20:17.920
He was released, but at the time of the attack, he took the impact of the bombardment.

00:20:17.920 --> 00:20:22.230
He suffered bruises all over his
body and has been hospitalized.

00:20:24.470 --> 00:20:25.980
I understand, Lt. Commander Yang.

00:20:26.620 --> 00:20:27.720
Regardless of
the circumstances...

00:20:27.720 --> 00:20:31.480
...it seems you are presently the
supreme commander of Planet Econia.

00:20:31.920 --> 00:20:33.840
Fulfill your obligation
as a commanding officer.

00:20:33.840 --> 00:20:34.490
Yes, sir.

00:20:36.080 --> 00:20:37.840
Do you understand ?

00:20:38.280 --> 00:20:43.620
In any case, if both of you are not alive at the time of my arrival...

00:20:43.620 --> 00:20:45.750
...I will assume that the
live one killed the other.

00:20:45.750 --> 00:20:48.840
Be sure to maintain
the order of the place.

00:20:49.530 --> 00:20:50.700
I will do my best.

00:20:51.420 --> 00:20:53.770
When should we
expect you, Commander ?

00:20:56.970 --> 00:20:58.530
Three days from now.

00:20:59.560 --> 00:21:00.670
We await your arrival.

00:21:18.450 --> 00:21:20.840
It's just an issue
of expediency.

00:21:21.610 --> 00:21:26.420
If I claim to be a secret
inspector, no one will believe it.

00:21:26.420 --> 00:21:29.460
It's a lie that's believable
because of you, Lt. Commander Yang.

00:21:30.530 --> 00:21:31.990
I'm thankful for that.

00:21:35.470 --> 00:21:37.100
Are you angry with
me, Lt. Commander ?

00:21:37.620 --> 00:21:39.370
No, I'm not angry.

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:43.020
I'm just thinking about when
Commander Murai arrives...

00:21:43.020 --> 00:21:45.620
...and what explanation I should
give to make the story believable.{Cohere}

00:21:46.950 --> 00:21:50.100
I wonder if he likes jokes ?

00:21:50.880 --> 00:21:55.100
From what I heard, he very much
loathes jokes and corruption.

00:21:55.900 --> 00:21:58.370
He's the personification
of rule and order.

00:21:59.620 --> 00:22:01.990
You got that impression
from across the screen ?

00:22:02.840 --> 00:22:04.230
I did.

00:22:04.880 --> 00:22:08.170
It's a rare case in which the first impression turns out to be true.

00:22:08.170 --> 00:22:10.880
I wonder if we can change it
to one of the more common cases.

00:22:12.830 --> 00:22:16.620
Strict people like
to stick to reason...

00:22:16.620 --> 00:22:19.250
...so if he sees that reason is on
our side of the circumstances...

00:22:19.250 --> 00:22:22.370
...he probably won't
judge us unjustly.

00:22:22.370 --> 00:22:23.360
Probably...

00:22:25.430 --> 00:22:28.200
As we say, justice is
on our side, Lt. Commander.

00:22:29.110 --> 00:22:31.200
I don't think it'll
turn out too badly.

00:22:31.690 --> 00:22:34.080
Besides, there's no point
in worrying about it.

00:22:34.920 --> 00:22:36.410
Sure. You're right.

00:22:39.000 --> 00:22:41.000
As Yang put his
worries behind him...

00:22:41.000 --> 00:22:44.020
...he first ordered expediting the
hospitalization of the injured...

00:22:44.020 --> 00:22:47.370
...and managing the
bodies of the dead.

00:22:47.810 --> 00:22:49.020
As for the damaged buildings...

00:22:49.020 --> 00:22:53.020
...they must be preserved as they were,
and as for the residents in the area...

00:22:53.020 --> 00:22:55.560
...he had to report that
there was no impending danger.

00:22:55.560 --> 00:23:00.830
Until Commander Murai's arrival, it seemed that the days of duress would continue.

00:22:58.260 --> 00:23:05.300
A Rebellion of Microscopic Size

